## Secure Implementation

### Tier 1: Critical Fix (5 minutes)
Add password validation before issuing token

```java
@PostMapping("/login")
public ResponseEntity<?> login(@RequestBody LoginRequest request) {
    User user = userRepository.findByUsername(request.getUsername());

    if (user != null) {
        // FIX: Validate password before issuing token
        if (!passwordEncoder.matches(request.getPassword(), user.getPassword())) {
            return ResponseEntity.status(401).body("Invalid credentials");
        }
        String token = jwtService.generateToken(user);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(new AuthResponse(token, user.getUsername()));
    }

    return ResponseEntity.status(401).body("Invalid credentials");
}
```

**What This Fixes:**
- ✅ Password is validated before authentication succeeds
- ✅ Uses Spring Security's `PasswordEncoder` for secure comparison
- ✅ Returns same error for non-existent user and wrong password (prevents enumeration)

**Limitations:**
- ❌ No rate limiting (brute force still possible)
- ❌ No audit logging (can't detect attack attempts)
- ❌ No MFA support

### Tier 2: Production Implementation (15 minutes)
Use Spring Security with proper authentication

```java
package com.example.auth;

import org.springframework.security.authentication.*;
import org.springframework.security.core.Authentication;
import org.springframework.security.core.AuthenticationException;
import org.springframework.security.crypto.password.PasswordEncoder;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;
import java.time.Instant;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/auth")
public class SecureAuthController {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SecureAuthController.class);
    private final AuthenticationManager authenticationManager;
    private final JwtTokenProvider jwtTokenProvider;
    private final AuditService auditService;

    @PostMapping("/login")
    public ResponseEntity<?> login(@RequestBody LoginRequest request) {

        try {
            // Use Spring Security's AuthenticationManager
            Authentication authentication = authenticationManager.authenticate(
                new UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(
                    request.getUsername(),
                    request.getPassword()
                )
            );

            // Authentication successful - password was validated by Spring Security
            String token = jwtTokenProvider.generateToken(authentication);

            auditService.logAuthenticationSuccess(
                request.getUsername(),
                request.getIpAddress(),
                request.getUserAgent()
            );

            log.info("Authentication successful for user: {}", request.getUsername());
            return ResponseEntity.ok(new AuthResponse(token, request.getUsername()));

        } catch (BadCredentialsException e) {
            auditService.logAuthenticationFailure(
                request.getUsername(),
                "INVALID_CREDENTIALS",
                request.getIpAddress()
            );

            log.warn("Authentication failed for user: {} - Invalid credentials", 
                request.getUsername());
            return ResponseEntity.status(401).body("Invalid credentials");

        } catch (DisabledException e) {
            auditService.logAuthenticationFailure(
                request.getUsername(),
                "ACCOUNT_DISABLED",
                request.getIpAddress()
            );
            return ResponseEntity.status(403).body("Account disabled");

        } catch (LockedException e) {
            auditService.logAuthenticationFailure(
                request.getUsername(),
                "ACCOUNT_LOCKED",
                request.getIpAddress()
            );
            return ResponseEntity.status(403).body("Account locked due to failed attempts");
        }
    }
}

@Service
public class CustomUserDetailsService implements UserDetailsService {

    private final UserRepository userRepository;
    private final PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder;

    @Override
    public UserDetails loadUserByUsername(String username) throws UsernameNotFoundException {
        User user = userRepository.findByUsername(username)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new UsernameNotFoundException("User not found"));

        return org.springframework.security.core.userdetails.User
            .withUsername(user.getUsername())
            .password(user.getPassword())  // Already bcrypt hashed
            .authorities(user.getRole())
            .accountExpired(false)
            .accountLocked(user.isLocked())
            .credentialsExpired(false)
            .disabled(!user.isEnabled())
            .build();
    }
}
```

**What This Adds:**
- ✅ Spring Security's `AuthenticationManager` handles password validation
- ✅ Comprehensive audit logging (success and failure)
- ✅ Proper exception handling (disabled accounts, locked accounts)
- ✅ Account lockout support after failed attempts
- ✅ Standardized error messages (prevent username enumeration)

### Tier 3: Enterprise Hardening (30 minutes)
Add rate limiting, MFA, and behavioral analytics

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/auth")
public class HardenedAuthController {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(HardenedAuthController.class);
    private final AuthenticationManager authenticationManager;
    private final JwtTokenProvider jwtTokenProvider;
    private final AuditService auditService;
    private final RateLimitService rateLimitService;
    private final MfaService mfaService;
    private final ThreatDetectionService threatService;

    @PostMapping("/login")
    public ResponseEntity<?> login(
            @RequestBody LoginRequest request,
            @RequestHeader("X-Forwarded-For") String ipAddress,
            @RequestHeader("User-Agent") String userAgent) {

        // Rate limiting check
        if (rateLimitService.isRateLimited(request.getUsername(), ipAddress)) {
            log.warn("Rate limit exceeded for user: {} from IP: {}", 
                request.getUsername(), ipAddress);
            auditService.logRateLimitExceeded(request.getUsername(), ipAddress);
            return ResponseEntity.status(429).body("Too many login attempts. Try again later.");
        }

        // Threat detection (unusual login location, device, time)
        ThreatLevel threat = threatService.assessLoginThreat(
            request.getUsername(),
            ipAddress,
            userAgent,
            Instant.now()
        );

        if (threat.getLevel() == ThreatLevel.HIGH) {
            log.warn("High-threat login attempt for user: {} - {}", 
                request.getUsername(), threat.getReason());
            auditService.logHighThreatAttempt(request.getUsername(), threat);
            // Require additional verification
            return ResponseEntity.status(403).body("Additional verification required");
        }

        try {
            // Primary authentication (username + password)
            Authentication authentication = authenticationManager.authenticate(
                new UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(
                    request.getUsername(),
                    request.getPassword()
                )
            );

            // Check if MFA is required
            if (mfaService.isMfaEnabled(request.getUsername())) {
                String mfaToken = mfaService.generateMfaChallenge(request.getUsername());
                return ResponseEntity.status(206).body(new MfaChallengeResponse(
                    mfaToken,
                    "MFA verification required"
                ));
            }

            // Generate JWT token
            String token = jwtTokenProvider.generateToken(authentication);

            // Log successful authentication
            auditService.logAuthenticationSuccess(
                request.getUsername(),
                ipAddress,
                userAgent,
                threat.getLevel().toString()
            );

            // Update user's last login
            userService.updateLastLogin(request.getUsername(), ipAddress, Instant.now());

            return ResponseEntity.ok(new AuthResponse(token, request.getUsername()));

        } catch (BadCredentialsException e) {
            // Increment failed attempt counter
            int failedAttempts = rateLimitService.recordFailedAttempt(
                request.getUsername(),
                ipAddress
            );

            // Lock account after threshold
            if (failedAttempts >= 5) {
                userService.lockAccount(request.getUsername(), "Exceeded failed login attempts");
                log.warn("Account locked for user: {} after {} failed attempts",
                    request.getUsername(), failedAttempts);
            }

            auditService.logAuthenticationFailure(
                request.getUsername(),
                "INVALID_CREDENTIALS",
                ipAddress,
                failedAttempts
            );

            return ResponseEntity.status(401).body("Invalid credentials");
        }
    }
}

@Service
public class ThreatDetectionService {

    public ThreatLevel assessLoginThreat(String username, String ip, 
                                        String userAgent, Instant loginTime) {
        List<String> reasons = new ArrayList<>();
        int riskScore = 0;

        // Check for unusual login location
        UserLoginHistory history = loginHistoryRepo.findByUsername(username);
        if (history != null && !history.hasRecentLoginFromIp(ip)) {
            reasons.add("New login location");
            riskScore += 30;
        }

        // Check for unusual login time
        if (isUnusualLoginTime(username, loginTime)) {
            reasons.add("Unusual login time");
            riskScore += 20;
        }

        // Check for suspicious user agent
        if (isSuspiciousUserAgent(userAgent)) {
            reasons.add("Suspicious user agent");
            riskScore += 40;
        }

        // Check if IP is on threat list
        if (threatIntelService.isKnownMaliciousIp(ip)) {
            reasons.add("Known malicious IP");
            riskScore += 60;
        }

        // Determine threat level
        ThreatLevel level;
        if (riskScore >= 70) {
            level = ThreatLevel.HIGH;
        } else if (riskScore >= 40) {
            level = ThreatLevel.MEDIUM;
        } else {
            level = ThreatLevel.LOW;
        }

        return new ThreatLevel(level, riskScore, reasons);
    }
}

@Service
public class RateLimitService {

    private final LoadingCache<String, AtomicInteger> loginAttempts;

    public RateLimitService() {
        this.loginAttempts = CacheBuilder.newBuilder()
            .expireAfterWrite(15, TimeUnit.MINUTES)
            .build(new CacheLoader<String, AtomicInteger>() {
                public AtomicInteger load(String key) {
                    return new AtomicInteger(0);
                }
            });
    }

    public boolean isRateLimited(String username, String ip) {
        String key = username + ":" + ip;
        int attempts = loginAttempts.getUnchecked(key).get();
        return attempts >= 10;  // 10 attempts per 15 minutes
    }

    public int recordFailedAttempt(String username, String ip) {
        String key = username + ":" + ip;
        return loginAttempts.getUnchecked(key).incrementAndGet();
    }
}
```

**What This Adds:**
- ✅ Rate limiting (per username + IP combination)
- ✅ Behavioral threat detection (unusual location, time, device)
- ✅ Account lockout after failed attempts
- ✅ Multi-factor authentication support
- ✅ Threat intelligence integration (malicious IP detection)
- ✅ Comprehensive logging with context

## Testing & Validation

```java
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
class AuthenticationSecurityTest {

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @Autowired
    private UserRepository userRepository;

    @Autowired
    private PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder;

    @BeforeEach
    void setup() {
        // Create test user with known password
        User user = new User();
        user.setUsername("testuser");
        user.setPassword(passwordEncoder.encode("correct-password"));
        user.setRole("USER");
        userRepository.save(user);
    }

    @Test
    void testVulnerableCodeBypassesAuthentication() {
        // This test should PASS on vulnerable code (proving the vulnerability)
        // It should FAIL on secure code (proving the fix works)

        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                .contentType("application/json")
                .content("{\"username\":\"testuser\",\"password\":\"wrong-password\"}"))
            .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());  // Secure code returns 401
    }

    @Test
    void testCorrectPasswordAuthenticates() {
        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                .contentType("application/json")
                .content("{\"username\":\"testuser\",\"password\":\"correct-password\"}"))
            .andExpect(status().isOk())
            .andExpect(jsonPath("$.token").exists())
            .andExpect(jsonPath("$.username").value("testuser"));
    }

    @Test
    void testWrongPasswordFails() {
        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                .contentType("application/json")
                .content("{\"username\":\"testuser\",\"password\":\"wrong-password\"}"))
            .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized())
            .andExpect(jsonPath("$.token").doesNotExist());
    }

    @Test
    void testNonExistentUserFails() {
        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                .contentType("application/json")
                .content("{\"username\":\"nonexistent\",\"password\":\"any-password\"}"))
            .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
    }

    @Test
    void testEmptyPasswordFails() {
        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                .contentType("application/json")
                .content("{\"username\":\"testuser\",\"password\":\"\"}"))
            .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
    }

    @Test
    void testRateLimitingActivates() throws Exception {
        // Attempt login 11 times (rate limit is 10)
        for (int i = 0; i < 11; i++) {
            MvcResult result = mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                    .contentType("application/json")
                    .content("{\"username\":\"testuser\",\"password\":\"wrong\"}"))
                .andReturn();

            if (i < 10) {
                assertEquals(401, result.getResponse().getStatus());
            } else {
                assertEquals(429, result.getResponse().getStatus());  // Rate limited
            }
        }
    }

    @Test
    void testAccountLockoutAfterFailedAttempts() throws Exception {
        // Attempt login 5 times with wrong password
        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
            mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                    .contentType("application/json")
                    .content("{\"username\":\"testuser\",\"password\":\"wrong\"}"))
                .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
        }

        // 6th attempt should indicate account is locked
        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/auth/login")
                .contentType("application/json")
                .content("{\"username\":\"testuser\",\"password\":\"correct-password\"}"))
            .andExpect(status().isForbidden())
            .andExpect(content().string(containsString("locked")));
    }
}
```

